  "Jonah remained in the belly of the great fish for three days and three nights.": "b333ebfe8a3d46c0",
  "remained": "3e118152331b5a04",
  "belly": "59067da166523e59",
  "From inside the fish, Jonah cried out to the Lord his God.": "ed11f71ee1e5b276",
  "cried out": "b150a9f625bc0f0a",
  "\"In my distress I called to the Lord, and he answered me.\"": "c72b22701297c0d9",
  "distress": "16e601ed6c846b43",
  "answered": "68c780cd132a0299",
  "\"I will keep my promise to you, O Lord.\"": "c35ec0a3e569cc7a",
  "keep": "6ca7ea2feefc88ec",
  "promise": "3513d9452af7c176",
  "Then the Lord commanded the fish, and it spit Jonah out onto the dry land.": "a5f59538534a5600",
  "A second time, the Lord said to Jonah, \"Arise, go to Nineveh, that great city.\"": "8ac2921363fd856c",
  "This time, Jonah obeyed and went to Nineveh.": "b6580e8153bd5120",
  "obeyed": "4d6922a98ce9c365",
  "He proclaimed throughout the city, \"In forty days, Nineveh will be overthrown!\"": "ed975ac34d5bebce",
  "proclaimed": "213d77f667d6c9c2",
  "overthrown": "adf4bd5652475e24",
  "The people of Nineveh believed Jonah's message and trembled.": "bc4041b83e4d985e",
  "believed": "2fda9fce9f8475b8",
  "message": "ab530a13e4591498",
  "trembled": "c426217a7cf2ab34",
  "Even the king rose from his throne and humbled himself.": "2eaa31d59c7ca2cc",
  "rose": "618d663af0f1ec88",
  "humbled": "7544e2b7c1d025c6",
  "Everyone repented and turned away from their evil ways.": "7400e224f2f535b9",
  "repented": "af198ddbe15b68d9",
  "turned away": "59ff7915b5c2604f",
  "evil": "b5c1fb2efc6d6b46",
  "When God saw what they had done, he relented and spared the city.": "ccad67f2610029e1",
  "relented": "0d159581fb3f357b",
  "spared": "7f60ed9448bd9d2a",
  "But Jonah was deeply displeased and became furious.": "9a168a3e45d75a7d",
  "displeased": "c0ba3b0ed468f896",
  "furious": "ab8e1efe40afa487",
  "He prayed, \"Lord, why did you show mercy to these people?\"": "1af518df706bb45b",
  "mercy": "4d51fd998fd3a724",
  "\"I knew you were merciful, and that is why I tried to flee.\"": "2b8cc8cef05b32ac",
  "merciful": "b7d504c1a60c9ac3",
  "Jonah left the city, sat east of it, and waited to see what would happen.": "b4097255c98c607c",
  "east": "6bdb262b0201799a",
  "happen": "9ecfb3a042a271f4",
  "The sun was burning, and Jonah grew weary.": "6c9e01df0287f82a",
  "burning": "5221409b64943f25",
  "weary": "1702a4bae332d66f",
  "The Lord caused a leafy vine to grow over Jonah, providing shade above his head.": "3f12d2c03a57b777",
  "caused": "35e1036abb38a08d",
  "vine": "3958765b23d8a51d",
  "providing": "ff2d2723391066d3",
  "Jonah was overjoyed by the cool shade of the vine.": "4479c98ef545cf53",
  "overjoyed": "961507f9af590660",
  "cool": "c34045c1a1db8d1b",
  "But the next morning, a worm attacked the vine and it withered.": "ca5ef49ae632b364",
  "worm": "b9af17af4fc5708e",
  "attacked": "64e591a71896718d",
  "withered": "8accd008cee2d379",
  "A scorching east wind blew, and Jonah grew faint under the burning sun.": "090456026ad5dca5",
  "scorching": "c198ea5d2d0a4f24",
  "faint": "4acfccfbec10ea28",
  "Jonah said, \"It would be better for me to die than to keep living.\"": "d7204d6ca3cce174",
  "would": "c6323a2117013ed6",
  "God said, \"You care about a vine that you did not plant or tend, that grew in a night and perished in a night.\"": "85896a6ce84b0a00",
  "care": "f9ed2b54fd72ac16",
  "tend": "4f0a1f5aef53e953",
  "perished": "7b4a45cee3ec81ec",
  "\"Should I not have compassion on the great city of Nineveh, with so many people in it?\"": "ce6d06de00fed881",
  "compassion": "b260e1abb566eb8b",
  "so many": "50c38dceb224971e",
  "Daniel was a man of excellent spirit who served the king with wisdom.": "b0cc205b6212eead",
  "excellent": "6d785acc7d4ce49f",
  "spirit": "a68999add325ba99",
  "wisdom": "7c68b70cea5555e5",
  "The king favored Daniel above all the others.": "ae395f585b2661b2",
  "favored": "530690114b41bdf1",
  "The king planned to set Daniel over the entire kingdom.": "6c311dc6b8e8a05f",
  "planned": "9b0f1b10aff55228",
  "entire": "260b27ca3018bc10",
  "But the other officials grew envious of Daniel.": "9c7f841c647edb87",
  "envious": "74c4a5de72fc1bba",
  "They schemed, \"How can we find a charge against Daniel?\"": "1454fbc5d2891218",
  "schemed": "6a6ebeeda99ea1dc",
  "charge": "97488fbab3282166",
  "They knew that Daniel prayed three times a day, every day.": "5383421a59a78126",
  "three times": "0e17c819392a0060",
  "So they devised a plan and approached the king.": "6ddfc697f4afaf53",
  "devised": "858b59ff9fce2bd2",
  "approached": "9de24f1b304730d0",
  "\"O great king, issue a new decree!\" they declared.": "0de47513b008a132",
  "issue": "4a502846d070e208",
  "decree": "ad51f678a270ec51",
  "declared": "f833228cb8681bbf",
  "\"For thirty days, no person shall offer prayer to any god or man except you.\"": "d579bae160ff99e6",
  "offer": "988180bf0c9328c9",
  "except": "b11279547bc49510",
  "\"Whoever breaks this decree shall be cast into the den of lions.\"": "3f92c78ea5afd7a8",
  "whoever": "bb5d54010a1c2cd3",
  "cast": "603705cc260e946d",
  "The king signed the decree, making it official.": "fb9242ca699fe49f",
  "official": "6896191a14f6c665",
  "When Daniel heard about the decree, he went home, opened his window toward Jerusalem, and prayed as he always did.": "de19b3c7f67707f9",
  "Jerusalem": "451ebbe3f76682c7",
  "always": "9cdc6c47aa193ae7",
  "The officials caught Daniel in prayer and rushed to inform the king.": "16d776ded2d42b1c",
  "caught": "a47a2e1872852966",
  "rushed": "f657ccb0235eb874",
  "inform": "ea07dcc807ffe0d6",
  "\"Daniel continues to pray to his God three times a day, ignoring your decree!\" they reported.": "bcbba7951497a7b4",
  "continues": "d83696c88df7a505",
  "ignoring": "2ea2189e7d33373a",
  "The king was deeply troubled, for he cared about Daniel.": "3b36c41cd21b7bde",
  "deeply": "0e9b99efef2f80fb",
  "troubled": "8e260bd854566e0d",
  "cared": "f25d0ff2ea91d45c",
  "Until sunset, the king sought a way to rescue Daniel, but the decree could not be reversed.": "47c0f8959a13a60d",
  "sunset": "0829103205fbe796",
  "rescue": "824ef7874151e9c8",
  "reversed": "bc64f64fb479ef52",
  "Finally, the king commanded that Daniel be cast into the den of lions.": "d53858284e3e6ea5",
  "finally": "205c3e16c66ff0b8",
  "The king said to Daniel, \"May your God, whom you serve continually, deliver you.\"": "570648ddd2e60c9d",
  "continually": "62849eb6914cf2d8",
  "deliver": "fa2dcc238152c873",
  "A massive stone was rolled over the entrance of the den and sealed.": "dcabb034d5b516c6",
  "massive": "6c7bbbc199d3b161",
  "rolled": "ffccf707bfaed5fb",
  "entrance": "3902eb874fcc6c8a",
  "That night, the king refused all food and could not sleep.": "9d5cf589b42999f8",
  "At the break of dawn, the king hurried to the den.": "e36ca69a2857a157",
  "dawn": "8326e09ce4e90a41",
  "hurried": "e448efe6f87bf782",
  "\"Daniel, servant of the living God, has your God been able to deliver you from the lions?\"": "36922abd668d11a4",
  "Daniel replied, \"My God sent his angel and shut the mouths of the lions. They have not harmed me.\"": "e719fd1e4ddfb0eb",
  "harmed": "9c60fd8b10226ed5",
  "Overjoyed, the king proclaimed throughout his kingdom, \"The God of Daniel is mighty and everlasting!\"": "0927a2f98cd472ef",
  "everlasting": "d92d5a817df7b98a",
  "Long ago, King Ahasuerus ruled over a vast kingdom in Persia.": "491d3aa2ee4a973c",
  "Ahasuerus": "df4bc87ed34810a3",
  "ruled": "01614af71f87a2c5",
  "kingdom": "6038ac4d789347a5",
  "One day, the king needed a new queen.": "63f2668d9a8a034e",
  "needed": "c0cea2dd285281f7",
  "queen": "a9c3c1f767450233",
  "His servants brought beautiful young women from every part of the kingdom.": "13ea335d3d1bb2df",
  "servants": "c2672dbab1d18b3a",
  "brought": "553f3e2340aa69a8",
  "beautiful": "c6a1427d7119cd3c",
  "Among them was a Jewish girl named Esther, raised by her cousin Mordecai after she lost her parents.": "02c757cebaf8a1e2",
  "Jewish": "24c22477e62eebee",
  "cousin": "42e20cbe942249d8",
  "raised": "d9325e0936a5cb48",
  "Mordecai told Esther, \"Do not tell anyone where you come from.\"": "288c2ce9464ba088",
  "Mordecai": "9cd031086bb0b9b3",
  "anyone": "12ed8d14a55fdb47",
  "The king loved Esther more than all the others, and he made her his queen.": "6a7abf8c734bb9ac",
  "loved": "98c1baa889465545",
  "others": "01db91d06032cc64",
  "made": "ea0890697a77af0a",
  "One day Mordecai overheard two men plotting to harm the king.": "cf21567801ffe80b",
  "overheard": "7ddd03b89cd95fec",
  "plotting": "50f59d43eca90d99",
  "harm": "af3ce03f6874c531",
  "Mordecai warned Esther, and Esther told the king.": "b6fd183bb9e3609b",
  "warned": "da0e6487d4b40612",
  "The king was saved, and Mordecai's name was written in the royal records.": "a57f996a0d986b9d",
  "saved": "d81c55f49c5bb0d3",
  "royal": "aa43038afb6314a3",
  "records": "a94e7bcfcbed3c84",
  "Later, the king promoted a man named Haman to the highest seat in the palace.": "5e7e8d44ce93f5f4",
  "Haman": "2a2f260da8b96a1b",
  "promoted": "348f71b67f2d7423",
  "palace": "ee2aa44805b51b10",
  "The king ordered everyone to bow down before Haman.": "b3387e293277e2b3",
  "ordered": "7fdbf2f7e97fe77a",
  "bow": "c177affdff64002e",
  "before": "6db7d803e74f1ffa",
  "But Mordecai would not bow. \"I bow only to God,\" he said.": "7307c068e412b1a0",
  "only": "f905b19542ed08c9",
  "When Haman saw this, he was filled with rage.": "599f3472a59622aa",
  "filled": "8a2f8bcb5572a89a",
  "rage": "e59389d9c8173527",
  "He devised a plan to destroy Mordecai and all his people.": "09b2f8de8712c6aa",
  "people": "c9022680f888674e",
  "When Mordecai heard the news, he was deeply distressed.": "0cb0df5c4aaa1332",
  "distressed": "d2621e35f42e62a7",
  "He sent a message to Esther, \"Go to the king and beg him to save our people.\"": "61136ddd1cacce30",
  "beg": "e80f71a8d7311927",
  "save": "157dca92e4250458",
  "Esther was afraid. \"Anyone who enters the king's room without being called may die.\"": "b5be314c264964de",
  "enters": "28faaa675ccec57f",
  "Mordecai answered, \"Perhaps you became queen for such a time as this.\"": "3bf7ee5bbc78c1bc",
  "perhaps": "1ba2ebb275e86668",
  "became": "3f5c81b45da7f1f2",
  "such": "a5c935d142e9fa6e",
  "Esther made up her mind. \"If I perish, I perish.\"": "4305460636913b3e",
  "mind": "1c48f6310f1c849b",
  "perish": "72d58a93377a8219",
  "For three days, she and all her people fasted and prayed together.": "a7eebc11c1fbaa34",
  "fasted": "5ab8702ac5e4315f",
  "prayed": "5a1f63fdc798f83f",
  "On the third day, Esther stood before the king. He held out his golden scepter.": "cd12e4a47180098f",
  "stood": "96cbf33afdf16e94",
  "golden": "dd56de4137951d9c",
  "scepter": "6d0f466fe3796207",
  "Esther invited the king and Haman to a banquet.": "c7f4a34a8b5bbd97",
  "invited": "307128ff4d35a7e2",
  "banquet": "f4549a19d61970ef",
  "That night, the king could not sleep. He asked for the old records to be read.": "38f0bcca61049b19",
  "sleep": "0afa5bb5d5f17879",
  "The records told how Mordecai had saved the king's life. \"What reward was given to him?\"": "4c416d170d91aeee",
  "life": "63bd7065ef1e165a",
  "reward": "7696fff84f26472a",
  "At the second banquet, Esther cried out, \"This man is trying to destroy us all!\"": "4eec63a7f63de293",
  "trying": "4dd6721b523ac6d7",
  "The king was furious, and Haman met his end on the very gallows he had built.": "5ec210005963f049",
  "gallows": "0ad79209461f3ea8",
  "built": "586a866f990ab55e",
  "The king issued a new decree, and Esther's people were all safe.": "382a0f2237147a8a",
  "issued": "c91a3cc769f870fd",
  "safe": "8b3369944dd2a3fa",
  "Ever since, the people celebrate Purim each year to remember this rescue.": "df17ab0537a396c2",
  "celebrate": "9c457a4c48c5fe75",
  "Purim": "7727e784b2bba5ef"
}
